# Idiot brackets and monadic blocks

` "Double-a list."
⟦ xs ⟧: xs map(* 2)

doubled: ⟦ 3 4 5 ⟧

` "Guillemet pair."
« ys »: ys reverse

reversed: « 1 2 3 »

ceiling: ⌈3.2⌉
floored: ⌊3.8⌋

products: { :for x: [1, 2], y: [10, 20] }.(x + y)

filtered: { :for x: [1, 2, 3, 4, 5], _: [x] filter(> 3) }.(x)

let-block: { :let a: 1 b: a + 1 }.b

` "Monadic bracket: a list monad."
⟪{}⟫: { :monad bind(m, f): m mapcat(f) return(v): [v] }

pairs: ⟪ x: [1, 2] y: [10, 20] ⟫.(x + y)

` "Bracket with a destructured parameter."
‹ [a, b] ›: a + b

summed: ‹ 3 4 ›
